{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1510648-could-beast-work-as-a-wod-game","id":1510648,"title":"Could Beast work as a WOd game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-03T16:46:37-07:00","id":1510648,"title":"Could Beast work as a WOd game?","content":"honestly i think it could. i'd make the following changes:<br /> <br /> 1) The Primordial Dream is part of the Umbra,all of the umbra not just a particular part of it.<br /> 2) The concept of the Dark Mother and how she created all scary monsters is enhanced and put front and center.<br /> 3)Kinship is still there but is not front and center mostly because is hard for the wod critters to get along,but there's lot of beasts who try to make their kind get along anyway.<br /> <br /> how would you fit Beast in the WoD if you were so inclined?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T17:13:34-07:00","id":1510651,"title":"","content":"Not really. All the efforts to make World crossover friendly never really worked on the whole-you really need a shared foundation for that to work- and because of that the semiotic basis of the Dark Mother just clashes into the universe's colliding metaphysics and power, and the unified Umbra's already a hot fucking mess to deal with on it's own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T17:20:48-07:00","id":1510652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1510648-could-beast-work-as-a-wod-game?p=1510651#post1510651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. All the efforts to make World crossover friendly never really worked on the whole-you really need a shared foundation for that to work- and because of that the semiotic basis of the Dark Mother just clashes into the universe's colliding metaphysics and power, and the unified Umbra's already a hot fucking mess to deal with on it's own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh that's too bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T19:24:16-07:00","id":1510658,"title":"","content":"Well, there's also the question of how much adaptation you want to do. Beast, as is, certainly doesn't work in the WoD. But there's a lot of space for something Beast-like. Now, how happy that would make WoD fans, or Beast fans, is questionable, because it would require some major changes to both to get to work, but in theory there are things you can do.<br /> <br /> So, unless you want to just say &quot;if it isn't going to be Beath: the Primordial transplanted, so I'm dropping it,&quot; the question would be what is important to you in what Beast is, since that's what's going to color Beast: the Something-Else to make for the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T19:40:04-07:00","id":1510659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1510648-could-beast-work-as-a-wod-game?p=1510658#post1510658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there's also the question of how much adaptation you want to do. Beast, as is, certainly doesn't work in the WoD. But there's a lot of space for something Beast-like. Now, how happy that would make WoD fans, or Beast fans, is questionable, because it would require some major changes to both to get to work, but in theory there are things you can do.<br /> <br /> So, unless you want to just say &quot;if it isn't going to be Beath: the Primordial transplanted, so I'm dropping it,&quot; the question would be what is important to you in what Beast is, since that's what's going to color Beast: the Something-Else to make for the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I assumed the question was separate from &quot;Do you think World of Darkness could do a mythic monster game of it's own?&quot; THe answer to that question is both &quot;Yes&quot; and &quot;I'd actually like to see what that would look like.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T20:21:23-07:00","id":1510660,"title":"","content":"oh! ok then! so... hmm.... a Mythical Moster game in the wod. Well here are aspects i'd like to maintain<br /> <br /> 1) The whole archetypal thing Beast does, Beast has the seven main fears of the human animal. This hypothetical Beast-Inspired wod game could have that, but it also could have splats based on the types of mythical monster that is seems around the world. The Brute, The Sneaky,The Otherwordly are the same thing but with a different focus.<br /> 2)The idea of an single mythical ancestor that unites them actually is pretty fun to me, so we could have some kind of that, probably wouldn't be Mommy dearest though.<br /> 3) I still kinda want to see some Umbra exploration.<br /> <br /> i'd like to you folx <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> an <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a><br /> How would you treat the theme of Fear in this one? would it have any ties to the consensus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T20:36:58-07:00","id":1510666,"title":"","content":"Take the Thallain and/or the Adhene from Dreaming, and implant something like the Paths of Enlightenment from Masquerade. This means that existing Thallain/Adhene would be replaced though. And the result wouldn\u2019t be quite changeling nor Beast, but it should be close enough\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T20:51:06-07:00","id":1510669,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the shitty/Leviathan take* that some people try to apply to Beast in Chronicles would probably be excellent fodder for World, given it's apocalyptic flavor and instant increased isolation from the format.<br /> <br /> *Cataclysmic monster bound up in individuals and have to wrestle with keeping them in check while also needing to rely on their bursting power against opposition.**<br /> **I'm not saying Leviathan is shitty for that reason, I'm saying it's a bad way to &quot;fix&quot; Primordial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-03-2023, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T21:07:24-07:00","id":1510671,"title":"","content":"i almsot forgot about the fangame leviathan. god i wish i had enough ideas make a fan game someday","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T21:08:10-07:00","id":1510672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1510648-could-beast-work-as-a-wod-game?p=1510666#post1510666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take the Thallain and/or the Adhene from Dreaming, and implant something like the Paths of Enlightenment from Masquerade. This means that existing Thallain/Adhene would be replaced though. And the result wouldn\u2019t be quite changeling nor Beast, but it should be close enough\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>how would paths fo enlighteninment fit in the matter,now i'm curious ;D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T23:25:45-07:00","id":1510682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1510648-could-beast-work-as-a-wod-game?p=1510672#post1510672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> how would paths fo enlighteninment fit in the matter,now i'm curious ;D</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember reading up on the Paths some time ago and going \u201cHuh, that\u2019s what Beasts do or would do.\u201d and moving on. Don\u2019t remember which one it was \u2014 that impression might be incorrect.<br /> <br /> That, and there\u2019s probably room to model the build-up of personal legend and Lair culminating in Inheritance in the upwards advancement of Paths and the hierarchy-of-sins and convictions. As-is, it\u2019d be a much more rigid thing than the typical CofD approach, but it\u2019s a start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T23:49:33-07:00","id":1510684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1510648-could-beast-work-as-a-wod-game?p=1510671#post1510671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i almsot forgot about the fangame leviathan. god i wish i had enough ideas make a fan game someday</div> </div> </div> </div>Good piece of advice, plan on making a good game first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T11:20:31-07:00","id":1510896,"title":"","content":"1. If you are going to force the origin, I think it can be very awkward, but it works if you put that the beasts, in fact, would be like a first creation of Gaia, before the Garou to be her protectors, which gave rise to the primordials, but as they were willing to devour everything she contained them, however, centuries more the Dark Mother, who would be like a living manifestation of nightmares, this already paralleling Changeling: the Dreaming, so she welcomed them being like a new mother for them, and released these creatures into the world using nightmares as a means of passage, the result of which is something half dreaming, half flesh, hence they hunger for fears, but are unaffected by banality or cold iron like the fairies, even though they are weaker than they were before, however they are still vulnerable to human beliefs due to their fae half, so certain individuals, heroes, are dangerous to them. It's well summarized, but I think it's possible to develop something from there.<br /> <br /> 2. As for how they act, I believe they are not suited to living in a complex society, but they can form groups to protect a hunting territory or join other supernaturals as an exchange of favors, vampires can use them as support during the day and mages can make use of their abilities.<br /> <br /> 3. This is something that came to mind, but what if they had no defined shape and we just had a given number of points to define their physical characteristics, like if they have wings, claws, big size, thick skin, amorphous body, accelerated metabolism, in which case families would only determine their weaknesses, birthright and change the cost of certain characters, for example: Anakim can acquire big size or giant size for free, or Ugallu can acquire wings at reduced costs.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T07:57:01-07:00","id":1510981,"title":"","content":"First I've only just started learning the Beast's lore so I could be very wrong with the following but this is how I would port it over. <br /> <br /> I think a lot of it will tie into what do you mean by &quot;work as a WoD game.&quot; WoD games generally don't work together too well to begin with, the Vampire creation belief is entirely at odds with the Garou beliefs. That means I'm okay with some contradictions, both across lines and within the line itself. <br /> <br /> I don't think you'd have too much of a difficult time finding justification for beasts in the various lines, Lilith is often called the Dark Mother and she can be a kinship tie to Vampire and to Mage.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is a bit harder to make work, you could just say Gaia is the Dark Mother but I'm not a fan of that. I think I would tie Beasts to the Wyrm, but not, exclusively to the corruption of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Imagine, for a moment the Wyrm is caught in the Weaver's web, unable to free itself. It feels the corruption changing it from its original purpose and in a fit of both balance and corruption it steals a bit of energy from the wyld to form beings meant to prey on itself.<br /> <br /> A different option but one that might work is that the Dark Mother wasn't necessarily a being but a time and action. For time beyond measure the Garou preyed upon humanity, they were the things that went bump in the night and with consequences that carry in the collective subconscious of mankind even through modern day. In the ancient past when the Wyld was strong whose to say those actions couldn't have birthed monsters of their own.<br /> <br /> The Primordial Dream is a bit harder to work in for me, I think I would want to tie that into the metaplots of the Apocalypse / Gehenna. The Garou have the whole &quot;dying race&quot; schtik going on and Vampires have the &quot;blood thinning out and generations getting weaker&quot; thing so I think I would be tempted to go the other direction, too many beasts, lairs are growing larger and larger, until it seems the world will be unable to sustain any more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T11:11:23-07:00","id":1511001,"title":"","content":"i'm tempted to make it beast have competing mythologies in the wod<br /> Beast 1 &quot;we came from the dark mother,and so did everyone else<br /> Beast 2 &quot;We did,and the dark mother is lilith&quot;<br /> Beast 3 &quot;Nah we're spawn of the triat&quot;<br /> <br /> I kinda imagine Beasts having tons of origins tied to different point of the larger wod cosmology","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T11:32:27-07:00","id":1511003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1510648-could-beast-work-as-a-wod-game?p=1511001#post1511001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i'm tempted to make it beast have competing mythologies in the wod<br /> Beast 1 &quot;we came from the dark mother,and so did everyone else<br /> Beast 2 &quot;We did,and the dark mother is lilith&quot;<br /> Beast 3 &quot;Nah we're spawn of the triat&quot;<br /> <br /> I kinda imagine Beasts having tons of origins tied to different point of the larger wod cosmology</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be kind of weird.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T12:29:09-07:00","id":1511010,"title":"","content":"Since Beasts are inherently creatures tied to dreams, on important thing to remember about them is the impact of the local Apex. The Apex does not need to be a Beast (and often isn't). The Apex is the strongest supernatural force in the local ecosystem such that it bends the local dream-state towards its inclinations.<br /> <br /> While Beasts are free to believe whatever about origins, on the ground what matters is the Apex. If the Apex is an ancient 4th Gen Noddist-believing vampire, the local dreamscape is going to be colored by that, and local Beasts are going to have to account for vampire truths in how they operate.<br /> <br /> It's not super easy on games with lots of different supernaturals running around, but in actual play it means that contradictions between how Beasts think things work, and how other supernaturals believe things work, and resolved rather handily by the fact that the most supernaturally impacting individual &quot;wins&quot; locally. A changeling Apex means Primodrial Pathways follow trods through the Dreaming, while a mage Apex means the Primordial Dream happens to be adjacent to the Astral High Realms.<br /> <br /> The Begotten can be as technically correct about the true history of the setting as you want, but part of their &quot;easy crossover&quot; setup is that it doesn't really matter to how individuals have to manage their lives. The greatest impact of the subconscious fears of the local human minds twists things beyond a Beast's control; being the eldest child doesn't mean you always get to pick how things are done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T10:00:56-07:00","id":1511077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1510648-could-beast-work-as-a-wod-game?p=1511003#post1511003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it would be kind of weird.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Would it be any weirder than a Noddist, a follower of Lilith, a Laibon, and a Settite all standing around arguing about where they come from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T10:47:57-07:00","id":1511078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1510648-could-beast-work-as-a-wod-game?p=1511077#post1511077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would it be any weirder than a Noddist, a follower of Lilith, a Laibon, and a Settite all standing around arguing about where they come from?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's easier for them to try to kill each other, but I get your point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T00:57:16-07:00","id":1512411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1510648-could-beast-work-as-a-wod-game?p=1511010#post1511010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Beasts are inherently creatures tied to dreams, on important thing to remember about them is the impact of the local Apex. The Apex does not need to be a Beast (and often isn't). The Apex is the strongest supernatural force in the local ecosystem such that it bends the local dream-state towards its inclinations.<br /> <br /> While Beasts are free to believe whatever about origins, on the ground what matters is the Apex. If the Apex is an ancient 4th Gen Noddist-believing vampire, the local dreamscape is going to be colored by that, and local Beasts are going to have to account for vampire truths in how they operate.<br /> <br /> It's not super easy on games with lots of different supernaturals running around, but in actual play it means that contradictions between how Beasts think things work, and how other supernaturals believe things work, and resolved rather handily by the fact that the most supernaturally impacting individual &quot;wins&quot; locally. A changeling Apex means Primodrial Pathways follow trods through the Dreaming, while a mage Apex means the Primordial Dream happens to be adjacent to the Astral High Realms.<br /> <br /> The Begotten can be as technically correct about the true history of the setting as you want, but part of their &quot;easy crossover&quot; setup is that it doesn't really matter to how individuals have to manage their lives. The greatest impact of the subconscious fears of the local human minds twists things beyond a Beast's control; being the eldest child doesn't mean you always get to pick how things are done.</div> </div> </div> </div>My own thought would be to juxtapose the Primordial Dream against the Dreaming: not that they echo each other in any way, anymore than the Dark Umbra of Wraith echos the Middle Umbra of Werewolf; but that, in terms of how the overall cosmology fits together, the Primordial Dream isn't \u201cthe Umbra as a whole\u201d; it's \u201cthe Shadow* of the Dreaming\u201d, a hitherto unexplored layer of the collective unconscious. That is, Beasts have their own \u201cplayground\u201d, the same way that Changelings, Werewolves, and Wraiths do; but as Heavy Arms said, Beasts are inherently tied to dreams \u2014 or rather, they're inherently tied to nightmares. <br /> <br /> Crossover with other gamelines doesn't come from Beasts rampaging all over the various layers of the Umbra; it comes from the Primordial Dream having ties to the monstrous aspects of the various denizens of the World of Darkness. To hear the Beasts tell it, a vampire's Hunger derives from the Primordial Dream, as does a werewolf's Rage, a wraith's Angst, and a changeling's Nightmares. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">* I'm attempting to invoke \u201cShadow\u201d as Jung used the term.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T12:30:12-07:00","id":1518442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1510648-could-beast-work-as-a-wod-game#post1510648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">honestly i think it could. i'd make the following changes:<br /> <br /> 1) The Primordial Dream is part of the Umbra,all of the umbra not just a particular part of it.<br /> 2) The concept of the Dark Mother and how she created all scary monsters is enhanced and put front and center.<br /> 3)Kinship is still there but is not front and center mostly because is hard for the wod critters to get along,but there's lot of beasts who try to make their kind get along anyway.<br /> <br /> how would you fit Beast in the WoD if you were so inclined?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a pretty easy one to map in, the dark mother can be mapped to lilith with a little extra added in and the primordial dream is the oldest parts of the deep umbra","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T12:55:49-07:00","id":1518774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1510648-could-beast-work-as-a-wod-game#post1510648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">honestly i think it could. i'd make the following changes:<br /> <br /> 1) The Primordial Dream is part of the Umbra,all of the umbra not just a particular part of it.<br /> 2) The concept of the Dark Mother and how she created all scary monsters is enhanced and put front and center.<br /> 3)Kinship is still there but is not front and center mostly because is hard for the wod critters to get along,but there's lot of beasts who try to make their kind get along anyway.<br /> <br /> how would you fit Beast in the WoD if you were so inclined?</div> </div> </div> </div>With some changes I guess it could fit?<br /> I'd make the Beasts into the Children populating Lilith's original Garden, and integrate them and their lessons in the mythos of the Bahari and Verbena.<br /> I might also make them a kind of Gallain or Thallain, with the primordial Dream being a part of the Dreaming.<br /> I'd shift the Lessons from being their purpose from their versions of a Bunk, and make their purpose the subornation of the other supernaturals thanks to Kinship, which would be just a mean to that end, instead of a proof of being related to others supernatural creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-25T16:26:28-07:00","id":1518789,"title":"","content":"Lessons aren't a Beast's purpose Lessons are something some Beasts do in order to give their existence a purpose since they don't get any overt mandate from the Dark Mother to do anything other than exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T11:19:26-07:00","id":1519351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1510648-could-beast-work-as-a-wod-game?p=1510671#post1510671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i almsot forgot about the fangame leviathan. god i wish i had enough ideas make a fan game someday</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to give the opposite piece of advice to Arcane arts. Plan on making a good game. The opposite side is, expect the first game you make will be bad. Then make a sligthly better game, and repeat until you are not making crap games anymore.<br /> <br /> Practice practice practice. Doesn't matter if the first game is a single page, make something even if it isn't perfect. Then improve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}